== Section A — Parties and pressure groups (Questions 1–8)

#mcq(1, [A political party is an organised group that seeks to],
  [provide welfare to members],
  [regulate the economy],
  [win power by contesting elections],
  [influence policy without office]
)

#mcq(2, [Which of the following is a function of a political party?],
  [Adjudicating disputes],
  [Conducting elections],
  [Issuing currency],
  [Recruiting and training political leaders]
)

#mcq(3, [A party with a large membership, branches and a written programme is a],
  [coalition],
  [mass party],
  [pressure group],
  [cadre party]
)

#mcq(4, [A party system in which two major parties alternate in government is called],
  [one-party],
  [multi-party],
  [two-party],
  [no-party]
)

#mcq(5, [Which of the following is a merit of a two-party system?],
  [It guarantees proportional representation],
  [It gives small parties the balance of power],
  [It offers a clear choice of alternative governments],
  [It requires coalition government]
)

#mcq(6, [A pressure group differs from a political party because a pressure group],
  [cannot hold meetings],
  [has no members],
  [does not seek to form a government],
  [cannot lobby]
)

#mcq(7, [The Nigeria Labour Congress is an example of],
  [a statutory corporation],
  [a sectional group],
  [a political party],
  [a promotional group]
)

#mcq(8, [Which of the following is a legitimate method of a pressure group?],
  [Nominating candidates for election],
  [Declaring a law unconstitutional],
  [Organising a peaceful demonstration],
  [Conducting a census]
)

== Section B — Elections and public opinion (Questions 9–19)

#mcq(9, [An election is a process by which],
  [laws are made],
  [the adult population chooses people to hold public office],
  [parties are registered],
  [the budget is approved]
)

#mcq(10, [The right to vote is called],
  [the mandate],
  [the franchise],
  [the plebiscite],
  [candidacy]
)

#mcq(11, [In Nigeria the franchise is granted to citizens who are],
  [aged eighteen and registered],
  [property owners],
  [literate in English],
  [taxpayers for five years]
)

#mcq(12, [A system in which the candidate with the highest vote wins, without needing a majority, is],
  [first past the post],
  [proportional representation],
  [the second ballot],
  [the alternative vote]
)

#mcq(13, [The main merit of proportional representation is that it],
  [allocates seats in proportion to votes cast],
  [is the simplest system to count],
  [always produces a strong majority],
  [abolishes constituencies]
)

#mcq(14, [Elections in Nigeria are conducted by],
  [the National Assembly],
  [the Ministry of Interior],
  [INEC],
  [the Supreme Court]
)

#mcq(15, [Which of the following is an electoral malpractice?],
  [Gerrymandering],
  [A secret ballot],
  [A public count],
  [A current register]
)

#mcq(16, [An election is most likely to be free and fair when],
  [the army announces the results],
  [only one party contests],
  [the ruling party controls the commission],
  [the commission is independent and the ballot is secret]
)

#mcq(17, [Public opinion is best described as],
  [the policy of the government],
  [the editorial policy of a newspaper],
  [the result of the last census],
  [the views of the adult population on public questions]
)

#mcq(18, [The mass media are called the fourth estate because they],
  [collect taxes],
  [scrutinise and inform the public and the government],
  [make the laws],
  [conduct elections]
)

#mcq(19, [A government that wins an election claims a mandate, which means],
  [authority to carry out the programme on which it campaigned],
  [the ownership of state property],
  [the legal right to rule],
  [immunity from the courts]
)

== Section C — Citizenship and rights (Questions 20–26)

#mcq(20, [Citizenship by birth in Nigeria requires that a person be born in Nigeria and],
  [have lived in Nigeria for fifteen years],
  [own property in Nigeria],
  [have a Nigerian passport],
  [have a parent or grandparent belonging to an indigenous community]
)

#mcq(21, [A foreign woman married to a Nigerian citizen may become a citizen by],
  [registration],
  [naturalisation],
  [descent],
  [birth]
)

#mcq(22, [Citizenship by naturalisation requires residence in Nigeria for],
  [five years],
  [twenty years],
  [fifteen years],
  [ten years]
)

#mcq(23, [Nigerian law permits],
  [dual citizenship for the diaspora only],
  [dual citizenship],
  [no dual citizenship],
  [dual citizenship for women only]
)

#mcq(24, [Which of the following is a fundamental human right in Nigeria?],
  [Right to employment],
  [Right to shelter],
  [Right to fair hearing],
  [Right to free university education]
)

#mcq(25, [A citizen whose right to liberty is breached may seek redress under],
  [section 6],
  [section 14],
  [section 46],
  [section 9]
)

#mcq(26, [The Public Complaints Commission is otherwise called the],
  [chief whip],
  [ombudsman],
  [attorney-general],
  [auditor-general]
)

== Section D — Administration and local government (Questions 27–34)

#mcq(27, [The civil service is described as permanent because],
  [it is elected],
  [it is funded by donors],
  [its officials cannot retire],
  [it continues through changes of government]
)

#mcq(28, [The civil service is controlled by the legislature mainly through],
  [the courts],
  [appropriation and committees],
  [the army],
  [appointment of permanent secretaries]
)

